      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "Even contest but BULLETPROOF BOY (5) is always a player in this type of race. Manners let him down when he travelled north for the Len Smith Mile last week but he had come from the back row to place in the Casey Classic here prior. Should get his chance from the front row. The recent form of SIR JIMMY (1) may not leap off the page but he has had a series of wider or second row barriers. He could be a big improver from the ace draw. YAMBUKIAN (3) found winning form in a weaker race here on Wednesday, leading from wider and cruising home. Stronger here but he is race fit now and can go forward again from a lower draw. FORTY LOVE (8) was far from disgraced from wider on this row last start and was racing consistently prior. Draws for a trail so could be competitive. JILLIBY NITRO (7) draws wider tonight but there was plenty of merit in the last-start second in the Casey Classic.",
